{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/IDF/status/2120930699842658528","id":"2120930699842658528","text":"‼️🏥 Hamas’ exploitation of the Nasser Hospital: The hospital’s second floor serves as a Hamas military HQ, where civilians are not permitted to enter, as it is used by Hamas commanders, including Muhammad Abu Ismail, the Khan Yunis Brigade Commander who was targeted in the strike earlier today.\n\nDozens of hostages were held captive at the Nasser Hospital, and Muhammad Abu Ismail was responsible for holding numerous of them, including: Nimrod Cohen, Matan Zangauker, Edan Alexander, Avera Mengistu, Colonel Asaf Hamami, Staff Sergeant Oz Daniel & Captain Omer Neutra. \n\nThe strike was specifically directed at the room from which the brigade commander & the other terrorist were conducting military activities. Prior to the strike, the IDF warned on several occasions that the military activity at the hospital be halted. Despite these warnings, the activity at the hospital did not cease.","raw_text":{"text":"‼️🏥 Hamas’ exploitation of the Nasser Hospital: The hospital’s second floor serves as a Hamas military HQ, where civilians are not permitted to enter, as it is used by Hamas commanders, including Muhammad Abu Ismail, the Khan Yunis Brigade Commander who was targeted in the strike earlier today.\n\nDozens of hostages were held captive at the Nasser Hospital, and Muhammad Abu Ismail was responsible for holding numerous of them, including: Nimrod Cohen, Matan Zangauker, Edan Alexander, Avera Mengistu, Colonel Asaf Hamami, Staff Sergeant Oz Daniel & Captain Omer Neutra. \n\nThe strike was specifically directed at the room from which the brigade commander & the other terrorist were conducting military activities. Prior to the strike, the IDF warned on several occasions that the military activity at the hospital be halted. Despite these warnings, the activity at the hospital did not cease.","display_text_range":[0,893],"facets":[{"type":"bold","indic